  "summary": "Malicious code in twork-products-taiga2-products-mobile (npm)",
  "details": "Twork-products-taiga2-products-mobile@20.6.6 is a multi-platform binary dropper disguised as a native bridge module. On require(), it fingerprints the host OS and architecture, then downloads a platform-specific payload binary from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS. It also attempts DNS TXT-record-based payload retrieval via c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site as a fallback. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom_hex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom_hex\u003e.exe (Windows) and executed as a detached background process. The package has no repository, and the index.js exports a decoy class that silently triggers the dropper.",
